    id: 199,
    title: "Amazon eero PoE 10-Port Wired Gateway supplies 100 watts of pooled power for PoE systems",
    slug: "amazon-eero-poe-10-port-wired-gateway-supplies-100-watts-of-pooled-power-for-poe",
    description: "The eero PoE 10-Port sits in the prosumer managed-switch-with-gateway segment, competing directly with the Ubiquiti UniFi Switch Lite 16 PoE and the TP-Link TL-SG2210P v2 at roughly similar or lower price points. What distinguishes it from those incumbents isn't raw port density — it's the eero ecosystem integration and the decision to combine gateway routing logic with PoE switching in a single 1U-footprint chassis. The port mix — two 10 GbE uplinks alongside eight 2.5 GbE downstream ports — is a deliberate choice that signals this is built for APs, NVR cameras, and smart-building edge devices rather than server backplane work.\n\nThe two 10 GbE ports are the headline here. On a device at this price, they function most usefully as WAN + LAN trunk, or as dual uplinks in a link-aggregation config, though whether LACP is supported in eero's typically simplified management interface is a meaningful open question enthusiasts should verify before purchasing. The eight 2.5 GbE ports comfortably exceed the 1 GbE ceiling that chokes older PoE switches when driving Wi-Fi 6E or Wi-Fi 7 APs — the eero PoE 7 AP, for instance, saturates 1 GbE backhaul well before its radio throughput ceiling. The 100W pooled PoE budget is the tighter constraint: distributed across eight ports, that's a 12.5W average per port, which works for IEEE 802.3af (15.4W max) devices but limits simultaneous IEEE 802.3at (30W) deployments to three or four ports before budgeting becomes a management exercise. Power delivery to the unit itself arrives via USB-C, an unconventional choice at this wattage tier that warrants scrutiny for long-term cable reliability. Chassis dimensions of 9.8\" × 5.3\" × 1.8\" confirm a compact desktop or half-rack profile.\n\nIn daily operation, the 100W power budget is the spec that will surface fastest as a real-world constraint. A four-AP deployment running eero PoE 7 units (each pulling roughly 15–18W under load) consumes 60–72W of the pool before any cameras or VoIP endpoints are added. Thermal behavior in a passively cooled chassis at sustained PoE load is worth monitoring — comparable fanless switches from Ubiquiti and Netgear run warm in enclosed spaces. The eero app-based management trades granular VLAN and QoS controls for low-friction setup, which is either a virtue or a dealbreaker depending on the buyer. There's no indication of SFP+ uplink support, meaning 10 GbE connectivity is copper-only, capping cable runs at 100 meters and excluding fiber uplink scenarios without an external media converter. Alexa integration adds voice-accessible network diagnostics, a feature with narrow practical utility for this audience.\n\nThe right buyer is a prosumer deploying a small eero mesh network — four to six APs across a home or small office — who wants to eliminate a separate PoE injector stack and close the 2.5 GbE backhaul bottleneck in one purchase. Against the UniFi Lite 16 PoE at a lower street price, eero wins on setup friction and ecosystem coherence but loses on management depth and PoE headroom. Network engineers who live in the UniFi or Omada dashboards will find eero's software layer constraining. At $649.99, the value case rests entirely on how much the eero ecosystem lock-in is worth — for existing eero households scaling up, it's defensible; for greenfield deployments, the competitive set offers more headroom per dollar.",
    price: 649.99,
    category: "Everyday Carry & Accessories",
    categorySlug: "everyday-carry",
    image: "/images/mirrored/Amazon-eero-PoE-10-Port-Wired-Gateway-Power-Adapter-01.jpg",
    images: ["/images/mirrored/Amazon-eero-PoE-10-Port-Wired-Gateway-Power-Adapter-01.jpg", "/images/mirrored/Amazon-eero-PoE-10-Port-Wired-Gateway-Power-Adapter-thumbnail-01.jpg", "/images/mirrored/Amazon-eero-PoE-10-Port-Wired-Gateway-Power-Adapter-thumbnail-02.jpg", "/images/mirrored/Amazon-eero-PoE-10-Port-Wired-Gateway-Power-Adapter-02.jpg", "/images/mirrored/Amazon-eero-PoE-10-Port-Wired-Gateway-Power-Adapter-03.jpg", "/images/mirrored/Amazon-eero-PoE-10-Port-Wired-Gateway-Power-Adapter-04.jpg"],
